discovery.querySketch:
TABLES:  SELECT TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME, TABLE_TYPE FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES WHERE TABLE_NAME != 'SYSTRANSCHEMAS' AND <schema filter>;
COLUMNS: SELECT TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME, COLUMN_NAME, ORDINAL_POSITION, CASE WHEN IS_NULLABLE='YES' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END, DATA_TYPE, CHARACTER_MAXIMUM_LENGTH FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS WHERE <same filter> ORDER BY TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME, ORDINAL_POSITION;
KEYS:    SELECT KCU.TABLE_SCHEMA, KCU.TABLE_NAME, KCU.COLUMN_NAME, KCU.ORDINAL_POSITION FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.KEY_COLUMN_USAGE KCU JOIN INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLE_CONSTRAINTS TCS ON <catalog/schema/name equality> WHERE TCS.CONSTRAINT_TYPE = 'PRIMARY KEY' AND <same filter> ORDER BY KCU.TABLE_SCHEMA, KCU.TABLE_NAME, KCU.ORDINAL_POSITION;
<schema filter> is either 'TABLE_SCHEMA IN (@p1, @p2, ...)' when advanced.discover_schemas is non-empty, or the four NOT-EQUAL exclusions otherwise. No sys.* views are queried.

incremental.querySketch:
single cursor column:
  SELECT * FROM [schema].[table] WHERE ([c1] > @p1) ORDER BY [c1];
two cursor columns (lexicographic keyset predicate, expanded per column):
  SELECT * FROM [schema].[table] WHERE ([c1] > @p1) OR ([c1] = @p1 AND [c2] > @p2) ORDER BY [c1], [c2];

